course: dictionary
lesson: 15834
title: Understood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Understood is the past tense of the verb understand. When you have got the meaning of something, you understood it. «Yesterday the puzzle was hard, but today I finally understood how it works.»
explain: Understood can also mean something is known or agreed without anyone needing to say it out loud. «It is understood that everyone walks in the corridor.» Nobody has to write that rule on the board, because everyone just knows it.
explain: On its own, Understood is a quick way to say «I understand, and I will do it.» If your teacher says, «Please put your coats away», you could answer, «Understood.» It shows you have heard and you are going to act.
fact: Understood is the past tense of understand: understand, understands, understood, understanding.
fact: «Understood» means knew or got the meaning of something.
fact: «It is understood that…» means something is accepted without needing to be said.
fact: «Make yourself understood» means getting other people to know what you mean.
fact: To show you have understood, explain the idea in your own words.
exercise: «Yesterday the puzzle was hard, but today I finally understood it.» What does understood mean here? | *Got the meaning of it | Forgot it completely | Lost it under a pile of books | Ran away from it
exercise: «It is understood that everyone walks in the corridor.» What does this sentence mean? | *Everyone knows and agrees without it being said | Nobody is allowed in the corridor | Everyone must shout it out loud
exercise: Which word is the past tense of understand? | understanding | *understood | understandable | understands
test: Mia asks, «Have you understood?» Her friend replies, «Understood!» What does the friend mean? | Please say it again more quietly | Nothing at all, it is a silly word | I am lost and need help | *I understand, and I will do it
test: Ravi says, «I tried to make myself understood in French.» What does he mean? | He spoke so quietly that nobody could hear | He wrote everything down in French | He forgot all his French words | *He tried to get others to know what he meant
exam: Which sentence uses understood correctly? | The bell has understood at three o'clock | The park understood its gate | *After the explanation, Sam understood how fractions work | Understood the cat is sleeping on the mat
